Did you get closer bearings?

00:33:47.400 --> 00:33:50.140
No, sir. We'd have to triangulate from ground vehicles in the area.

00:33:51.080 --> 00:33:51.420
Devante.

00:33:52.870 --> 00:33:53.750
Where's the nearest transporter?

00:33:54.440 --> 00:33:55.000
of the Atlantic.

00:33:55.370 --> 00:33:56.090
100 miles out.

00:34:00.540 --> 00:34:01.360
Coming in from New York.

00:34:01.690 --> 00:34:02.090
Yes, sir.

00:34:03.900 --> 00:34:05.920
I thought that wasn't supposed to take up until 1400 hours.

00:34:06.300 --> 00:34:09.460
Well, that's correct, sir, but it's been on route for 50 minutes, Commander Straker's orders.

00:34:10.900 --> 00:34:11.520
You must be psychic.

00:34:27.060 --> 00:34:27.220
Let's go.

00:34:27.990 --> 00:34:28.650
Evacuate!

00:34:33.450 --> 00:34:34.490
Open inner hatch.

00:34:34.950 --> 00:34:36.030
Opening in a hat

00:34:36.870 --> 00:34:37.830
In a hatch open.

00:34:42.310 --> 00:34:44.810
I want these shots developed and rated to control as soon as possible.

00:34:45.190 --> 00:34:45.710
How'd it look?

00:34:46.380 --> 00:34:48.920
Part of the metallic structure had practically been vaporized.

00:34:49.450 --> 00:34:50.090
I'll tell you one thing.

00:34:50.500 --> 00:34:52.700
It had been fired on by something before it crashed.

00:35:48.420 --> 00:35:49.900
Captain Collin just radioed these in.

00:36:02.170 --> 00:36:04.890
There's no doubt about it. That UFO was damaged before it crashed.

00:36:05.460 --> 00:36:06.120
But by what?

00:36:11.380 --> 00:36:12.300
You foes are sighted.

00:36:12.820 --> 00:36:14.960
One veers off, the other crashes off Western Ireland.

00:36:16.020 --> 00:36:18.580
And from the same area, someone breaks in on our wave band.

00:36:22.330 --> 00:36:23.270
Let's make a couple of guesses.

00:36:24.280 --> 00:36:25.680
An alien survives the crash.

00:36:26.360 --> 00:36:27.120
Goes into a house.

00:36:28.020 --> 00:36:29.320
The occupant is an old lady.

00:36:30.760 --> 00:36:31.660
She said she was blind.

00:36:31.960 --> 00:36:35.670
Yeah, so she thinks he's a man, an intruder possibly.

00:36:35.910 --> 00:36:39.760
The alien sets up a transmitter and beams in on our wave band.

00:36:41.490 --> 00:36:41.670
Why?

00:36:43.400 --> 00:36:44.960
Well, we'll know that better when we track it down.

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:48.290
Well, that won't be easy, Alec.

00:36:48.780 --> 00:36:51.660
With mobiles in the area, we can pinpoint his exact position.

00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:53.640
Yeah, so that'll take time.

00:36:54.120 --> 00:36:56.950
Less than an hour. Transporter will be there within minutes.

00:36:58.090 --> 00:36:59.510
Mobiles can be in the area immediately.

00:37:00.440 --> 00:37:01.220
And once they're in position,

00:37:02.460 --> 00:37:04.320
We can get exact bearings from his next transmission.

00:37:05.880 --> 00:37:06.640
A transporter.

00:37:08.540 --> 00:37:09.260
The one from New York.

00:37:10.390 --> 00:37:11.550
You ordered an early take-off.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:15.080
What have you done?

00:37:16.180 --> 00:37:17.240
I diverted it. What else?

00:37:20.980 --> 00:37:21.500
Is something wrong?

00:37:26.810 --> 00:37:28.990
I'll tell Captain Carlin to go ashore as field commander.

00:38:00.760 --> 00:38:01.240
Some coffee.

00:38:01.720 --> 00:38:02.220
Thank you.

00:38:02.970 --> 00:38:03.950
What time is it?

00:38:04.340 --> 00:38:05.300
That clock is right.

00:38:13.690 --> 00:38:14.370
hasn't arrived yet.

00:38:38.540 --> 00:38:42.220
A Block, Mrs Rutland, it's for you.

00:38:42.620 --> 00:38:44.500
No, I'll take it.

00:38:52.300 --> 00:38:55.920
Hello? Yes, it's me.

00:39:00.540 --> 00:39:01.160
Just the same.

00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:03.120
Cheers.

00:39:03.510 --> 00:39:04.170
It's been a delay.

00:39:06.070 --> 00:39:07.890
The drug will be here as soon as possible.

00:39:10.390 --> 00:39:10.790
Yes, I know.

00:39:11.580 --> 00:39:12.020
I know.

00:39:14.550 --> 00:39:16.070
I'd like to explain to Mary.

00:39:31.660 --> 00:39:32.160
It's been delayed.

00:39:35.200 --> 00:39:46.680
Yes, and your own son's life.

00:39:47.740 --> 00:39:50.300
Listen, Mary, please, it's not like that.

00:39:51.130 --> 00:39:51.950
You don't understand.

00:39:58.430 --> 00:39:59.750
Mary, listen to me.

00:40:01.530 --> 00:40:01.890
Mary.

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:41.800
Where's the transporter?

00:40:42.820 --> 00:40:43.860
Just landed in Ireland, sir.

00:40:44.610 --> 00:40:46.810
The second it's unloaded, I want it back in the air for London.

00:40:47.080 --> 00:40:47.420
Yes, sir.

00:41:13.850 --> 00:41:16.510
I'm sorry about the transport. Was it important?

00:41:16.690 --> 00:41:21.140
These things are always a question of priorities.

00:41:21.520 --> 00:41:25.840
Tell the mobiles not to move in until I give the word.

00:41:27.300 --> 00:41:28.960
Get me a large-scale map of the area.

00:41:29.100 --> 00:41:29.520
Yes, sir.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.760
Captain Carlin.

00:41:31.210 --> 00:41:31.610
Sir.

00:42:08.160 --> 00:42:16.410
It's all right, Billy. Our visitor's a nice man. He doesn't want to hurt us. It's all right, Billy.

00:42:27.800 --> 00:42:28.860
Mobile one in position.

00:42:29.450 --> 00:42:29.850
Roger one.

00:42:30.440 --> 00:42:35.750
All mobile's in position, sir. All we can do now is wait for the next transmission.

00:42:43.450 --> 00:42:52.690
An alien wants to cooperate. Help. Why else would he transmit on our wave band?

00:42:54.500 --> 00:42:57.500
Why won't you speak to me? Get a bearing.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.820
Why don't you tell me who you are?

00:43:03.520 --> 00:43:04.890
You can kill someone.

00:43:06.760 --> 00:43:08.300
What the devil's telling me that signal?

00:43:14.110 --> 00:43:16.210
Second UFO resighted.

00:43:16.960 --> 00:43:18.300
Moonbase red alert.

00:43:19.320 --> 00:43:20.900
Interceptors, immediate launch.

00:43:36.460 --> 00:43:37.840
Missile firing, minus six.

00:43:37.960 --> 00:43:38.630
Death of all.

00:43:48.360 --> 00:43:49.500
Interception negative.

00:43:50.140 --> 00:43:52.000
UFO proceeding to Earth.

00:43:53.250 --> 00:43:55.390
Red alert, replacement Sky One.

00:44:20.500 --> 00:44:21.040
to control.

00:44:21.560 --> 00:44:22.280
Vector one, three.

00:44:22.650 --> 00:44:23.270
Decimal 3.

00:44:24.760 --> 00:44:25.680
the mobiles to move in.

00:44:25.980 --> 00:44:26.320
Yes, sir.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:30.980
We'll be right back.

00:45:10.070 --> 00:45:11.010
Mobile one to control.

00:45:11.830 --> 00:45:12.850
8 miles from target.

00:47:17.820 --> 00:47:18.300
He told us everything.

00:48:14.260 --> 00:48:14.460
Harry.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:30.040
You

00:48:33.100 --> 00:48:33.300
Woo!
